{
  "name": "Schedule social media posts from a Google Sheets content calendar with PostWire",
  "nodes": [
    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## Run your content calendar from a Google Sheet\nFor social media managers and small teams who plan in a spreadsheet. Write an idea, the networks and a date in a row, mark it ready, and it is scheduled — with a different post written for each network.\n\n### How it works\n1. **Every morning at 8** the workflow reads rows whose status is ready.\n2. **Only future dates** skips rows whose time has passed.\n3. **PostWire** schedules each row. The connections and the text are checked now, so a problem shows up today, not at publishing time.\n4. **Mark row as scheduled** writes the status and the PostWire ID back to the sheet.\n\n### Setup\n1. Install the **PostWire** community node (Settings → Community nodes → `n8n-nodes-postwire`), then create a free account at postwire.io, connect your networks and paste the API key into a **PostWire API** credential.\n2. Create a sheet with the columns idea, networks (for example: linkedin, facebook, bluesky), publish_at (ISO date such as 2026-10-01T09:00:00-05:00), status and postwire_id.\n3. Connect Google Sheets and pick the sheet in both Sheets nodes.\n\n### Customize\nChange the trigger hour, add a Brand Voice, or add an image column and set Media to URL.\n\n*Uses a community node, so it runs on self-hosted n8n.*",
        "height": 651,
        "width": 520
      },
      "id": "45894f68-60fd-430e-adee-89095201a6b1",
      "name": "Sticky Note",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        -633,
        -97
      ]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## 1. Rows marked ready\nDaily read of the calendar.",
